{"title":"Eibach Develops Lightweight, Precision-Tuned MTB Coil Springs","link":"https://bikerumor.com/eibach-mtb-coil-springs/","date":1793895726000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-1-1536x1152.jpg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" alt=\"eibach mountain bike springs at sema 2026.\" /></p>\n<p>Eibach is a leader in performance car and off-road suspension, especially popular for track and desert racers. Soon, they want to bring that same performance to mountain bikers.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The new range of coil springs will be made in the USA, just like their automotive springs. But they’ll be sold as a kit with custom spring seats from German suspension performance brand <a href=\"https://radsporttechnik-lorey.de/?utm_source=bikerumor\" target=\"_blank\">Lorey</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-4.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-4.jpg\" alt=\"eibach mountain bike springs shown on a shock.\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-4.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-4-297x223.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-4-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-4-120x90.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-4-768x576.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-4-1200x900.jpg 1200w\" /></a><figcaption>All photos ©Tyler Benedict</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>For the springs, Eibach has two benchmarks: be the lightest in class, and offer the best tuning range. For weight, it’s a matter of using their decades of experience turning steel wire into springs. And they admit, it’s a goal, but that getting the performance right matters more than being the absolute lightest-weight coils on the market. Regardless, expect them to be among the lightest.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-3.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-3.jpg\" alt=\"eibach mountain bike springs at sema 2026.\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-3.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-3-297x223.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-3-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-3-120x90.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-3-768x576.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-3-1200x900.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>For tuning, they’re aiming for 20lb increments. Meaning, they’ll offer spring rates of 200lb/in, 220lb/in, 240lb/in, etc., up to 500lb/in or more to meet market demand.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Compare that to the standard 50lb increments from stock options by RockShox, Fox, and Cane Creek. Even current high-end aftermarket springs typically come in 25lb increments. Dropping that to 20lb increments gives you much finer tunability. A range of lengths will be available to fit popular shock stroke lengths, too.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-6.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1500\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-6.jpg\" alt=\"eibach mountain bike springs shown on a shock.\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-6.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-6-297x223.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-6-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-6-120x90.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-6-768x576.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-6-1200x900.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>For the perches, Lorey’s precision-machined spring seats thread onto popular shock bodies from Fox, Rockshox, etc. In this case, they’re custom-mated to Eibach’s springs for an exact fit, cradling the coil and keeping it rock solid top and bottom.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-7.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-7-1536x1152.jpg\" alt=\"eibach mountain bike springs at sema 2026.\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-7-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-7-297x223.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-7-120x90.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-7-768x576.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-7-1200x900.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-7.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-5.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1099\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-5-1536x1099.jpg\" alt=\"info card for eibach mountain bike springs.\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-5-1536x1099.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-5-297x213.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-5-120x86.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-5-768x550.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-5-1258x900.jpg 1258w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-5.jpg 1800w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-2.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-2-1536x1152.jpg\" alt=\"eibach mtb springs on a bike at SEMA Show.\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-2-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-2-297x223.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-2-120x90.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-2-768x576.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-2-1200x900.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/eibach-mtb-mountain-bike-coil-springs-2.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Beyond this info, details are sparse. There’s no set pricing or release date, but their reps told me they’re very close to production. Look for them (hopefully) in early 2027.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em><a href=\"https://eibach.com/mtb\" target=\"_blank\">Eibach.com/MTB</a></em></p>","author":"Tyler Benedict","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/eibach-mtb-coil-springs/#respond","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"0a31e1227fb1c0801f15b76506e9279a1da054af3ae92d6a62c7792ef3674c1c","category":"Cycling"}